From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] preprocessor: consume the newline after a line continuation

get_line() recognised a trailing backslash as a line continuation but left
the newline in the stream, so the continued line began with a stray newline.
Multi-line macro definitions -- pervasive in real kernel headers -- were
therefore mis-tokenised. Consume the newline.
---
--- a/src/preprocessor/preprocessor.cpp
+++ b/src/preprocessor/preprocessor.cpp
@@ -548,6 +548,8 @@
 					putback('\\');
 					return;
 				}
+				// Consume the newline after backslash (line continuation)
+				get();
 			}
 			c = peek();
 		}
